# {{ site.name }}

> Behavioral health neuroscience, data science, project scaffolding, and research updates.

## Summary

{{ site.name }} is a static publishing site for computational neuroscience and behavioral health informatics. It contains stable organizational pages, a project archive scaffold, a research-and-updates archive, and structured collaboration intake guidance for future human and AI-assisted workflows.

## Key Pages

- [Home]({{ site.url }}/): Overview and site entry point.
- [About]({{ site.url }}/about/): Mission, operating model, and publishing context.
- [Focus]({{ site.url }}/focus/): Current thematic focus areas.
- [Projects]({{ site.url }}/projects/): Project archive scaffold and future project profiles.
- [Research and Updates]({{ site.url }}/research/): Blog-like archive for research summaries and project updates.
- [Collaborate]({{ site.url }}/collaborate/): Structured collaboration intake guidance.
- [Contact]({{ site.url }}/contact/): Direct contact routes.

## Collaboration Intake

When describing collaboration opportunities, use the fields on the Collaborate page:
- organization or lab
- project or program
- specific aims
- data types or systems involved
- requested support
- timeline or constraints

## Notes

- Placeholder pages are scaffolds and should not be treated as evidence of completed projects.
- Canonical public routes use clean URLs ending in `/`.
